(2486806, 339121, 51900, '<td valign="top">it''s getting old.</td>', 'it''s getting old.', '2006-06-05 15:13:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486856, 340660, 56828, '<td valign="top">Besides having a very nice and sharp photo, you deserve high marks just for the effort.</td>', 'Besides having a very nice and sharp photo, you deserve high marks just for the effort.', '2006-06-05 15:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486904, 338771, 56828, '<td valign="top">almost saw a little too much.  Great for the light source...would have been even better in the shadows challenge.</td>', 'almost saw a little too much.  Great for the light source...would have been even better in the shadows challenge.', '2006-06-05 15:54:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486919, 340563, 6999, '<td valign="top">A simple photograph of a bottle of whisky - I don''t understand why this is ever going to be very interesting. Those blue and red reflections speak obviously of ambient light in a room, and suggest another light source than that bright glare on the lower part of the bottle, so arguably this doesn''t even fit the challenge instruction. I''m sorry to be harsh, but I don''t even see what you thought the apeal of this image might be.</td>', 'A simple photograph of a bottle of whisky - I don''t understand why this is ever going to be very interesting. Those blue and red reflections speak obviously of ambient light in a room, and suggest another light source than that bright glare on the lower part of the bottle, so arguably this doesn''t even fit the challenge instruction. I''m sorry to be harsh, but I don''t even see what you thought the apeal of this image might be.', '2006-06-05 16:02:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486926, 339092, 6999, '<td valign="top">There seems to be a resurgence of the glass chess-set shot here - it went away fro a year or so. I wonder if you were trying for a kind of ''Leica Glow'' around that highlighted King - but what has happened here just makes it seem over-exposed rather than luminous; it''s one of those areas where digital, I think, really loses out to film - over-exposure almost always just looks like a mistake.</td>', 'There seems to be a resurgence of the glass chess-set shot here - it went away fro a year or so. I wonder if you were trying for a kind of ''Leica Glow'' around that highlighted King - but what has happened here just makes it seem over-exposed rather than luminous; it''s one of those areas where digital, I think, really loses out to film - over-exposure almost always just looks like a mistake.', '2006-06-05 16:05:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486928, 340777, 45004, '<td valign="top">I like the almost abstract look the light creats in this image.</td>', 'I like the almost abstract look the light creats in this image.', '2006-06-05 16:06:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486940, 339433, 6999, '<td valign="top">Intriguing; very strong graphically, although i wonder about the black border - useful at the top of frame, perhaps, but the un-exoected cut-off at the bottom is perhaps more intrusive than i think you intended. There''s also a graininess - a very fine graininness, but nevertheless present - which to my eye doesn''t quite fit with the highly-controlled set-up here. It might just be a black--point theshold thing - the descent into pure black from the mid-tones seems very sudden, looking carefully at the stems of the blooms, and that makes the tonal graduations of the more shaded areas of the flowers lack that sense of smoothness.</td>', 'Intriguing; very strong graphically, although i wonder about the black border - useful at the top of frame, perhaps, but the un-exoected cut-off at the bottom is perhaps more intrusive than i think you intended. There''s also a graininess - a very fine graininness, but nevertheless present - which to my eye doesn''t quite fit with the highly-controlled set-up here. It might just be a black--point theshold thing - the descent into pure black from the mid-tones seems very sudden, looking carefully at the stems of the blooms, and that makes the tonal graduations of the more shaded areas of the flowers lack that sense of smoothness.', '2006-06-05 16:09:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486944, 340635, 6999, '<td valign="top">The highlights certainly give a sense of shininess, but are perhaps too disparate to make for a clean enough image to suit the simplicity of the composition, making for a visual paradox which detracts from the impact of this image. This kind of abstraction was never up my street, so I may not be your best judge, but I think it at least needs a stronger sense of texture, otherwise it may as well be simple design.</td>', 'The highlights certainly give a sense of shininess, but are perhaps too disparate to make for a clean enough image to suit the simplicity of the composition, making for a visual paradox which detracts from the impact of this image. This kind of abstraction was never up my street, so I may not be your best judge, but I think it at least needs a stronger sense of texture, otherwise it may as well be simple design.', '2006-06-05 16:11:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486957, 340633, 6999, '<td valign="top">Cunning, but not cunning enough? Given the light source you''ve shown us, I''m intrigued as to how the left side of that skull is more brightly lit than the right. But whatever. I do think,. however,m that you have the basis of a nice shot here - only there''s perhaps too much shadow, really, and your placing of that light source in frame is uncomfortable - not the fact that it''s there, but that it interrupts the lines of the skeleton so much, rather than seeming remote from it, like illumination should be - alongside the head like this, it looks like something you just couldn''t get out of frame, which carries an implication of laziness, rather than of artistic choice. Had you placed that light top right, and even reduced the size of the skeleton part of the image, which would have allowed you to brighten it a touch more, make it a touch less violently high-contrast, I think you''d generate more of an impression of the bones actually being lit by that light.</td>', 'Cunning, but not cunning enough? Given the light source you''ve shown us, I''m intrigued as to how the left side of that skull is more brightly lit than the right. But whatever. I do think,. however,m that you have the basis of a nice shot here - only there''s perhaps too much shadow, really, and your placing of that light source in frame is uncomfortable - not the fact that it''s there, but that it interrupts the lines of the skeleton so much, rather than seeming remote from it, like illumination should be - alongside the head like this, it looks like something you just couldn''t get out of frame, which carries an implication of laziness, rather than of artistic choice. Had you placed that light top right, and even reduced the size of the skeleton part of the image, which would have allowed you to brighten it a touch more, make it a touch less violently high-contrast, I think you''d generate more of an impression of the bones actually being lit by that light.', '2006-06-05 16:16:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486966, 340293, 45004, '<td valign="top">I like the detail on this shot. The lighting is very nice and rely help bring out the dew on the grass.</td>', 'I like the detail on this shot. The lighting is very nice and rely help bring out the dew on the grass.', '2006-06-05 16:19:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486971, 338696, 45004, '<td valign="top">I feel the light is too hot on his forehead and nose and it could use a small amount of fill in the shadows.</td>', 'I feel the light is too hot on his forehead and nose and it could use a small amount of fill in the shadows.', '2006-06-05 16:20:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486974, 340261, 45004, '<td valign="top">The grain is some what bothersome to me. I feel it is too much and lessens the quality and feel of the image. I do like the lighting and posing.</td>', 'The grain is some what bothersome to me. I feel it is too much and lessens the quality and feel of the image. I do like the lighting and posing.', '2006-06-05 16:22:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486980, 339427, 6999, '<td valign="top">Culturally, I think the inevitable priapic comparison is begged here; i''m not sure i want to go into that though. However technically, there''s the sense of slight channel clipping in some of the solid yellow areas, and of a fake element to the light intensity to image left. That channel clipping is what gives the more solid yellow areas a sense of missing detail, when the focus is definitely spot-on.</td>', 'Culturally, I think the inevitable priapic comparison is begged here; i''m not sure i want to go into that though. However technically, there''s the sense of slight channel clipping in some of the solid yellow areas, and of a fake element to the light intensity to image left. That channel clipping is what gives the more solid yellow areas a sense of missing detail, when the focus is definitely spot-on.', '2006-06-05 16:24:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486986, 339566, 45004, '<td valign="top">I like this image, but feel it has a strong feel of studio lighting. The color and intensity of light does not make me think of early morning. I do like the angle of the light and the streeks in the fog. The reflection is wonderful, almost dreamy.</td>', 'I like this image, but feel it has a strong feel of studio lighting. The color and intensity of light does not make me think of early morning. I do like the angle of the light and the streeks in the fog. The reflection is wonderful, almost dreamy.', '2006-06-05 16:25:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2486995, 339147, 45004, '<td valign="top">I feel the back light is too strong and the edges of the bottle are being lost. I also wopuld like to see more light on the front. The front label is not straight or need more angle.</td>', 'I feel the back light is too strong and the edges of the bottle are being lost. I also wopuld like to see more light on the front. The front label is not straight or need more angle.', '2006-06-05 16:28:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487003, 340770, 45004, '<td valign="top">I like the angle on this image. B&amp;W lends it self well to the truck.</td>', 'I like the angle on this image. B&W lends it self well to the truck.', '2006-06-05 16:32:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487012, 340186, 45004, '<td valign="top">A very creative look at a dandelion. Alomosy electrical.</td>', 'A very creative look at a dandelion. Alomosy electrical.', '2006-06-05 16:35:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487026, 339534, 45004, '<td valign="top">I think I would have liked the gun to have slightly more angle to make it read better. I do like the lighting and how it draws your eye into the shot.</td>', 'I think I would have liked the gun to have slightly more angle to make it read better. I do like the lighting and how it draws your eye into the shot.', '2006-06-05 16:42:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487036, 340025, 56828, '<td valign="top">Challenge related: The challenge was a single artificial light source and in the photo you can see several light sources.  You probably shoul dhave found a way to darken that area to make it seem as if the spot light was the only source of light.<br/> <br/>Technical:  The photo is very blurry and I can''t tell if you did this on purpose to hide the musicians face or if it was an accident while taken at a concert.  The left side of the photo has a couple of random bright spots that could have been cropped out as well.</td>', 'Challenge related: The challenge was a single artificial light source and in the photo you can see several light sources.  You probably shoul dhave found a way to darken that area to make it seem as if the spot light was the only source of light. Technical:  The photo is very blurry and I can''t tell if you did this on purpose to hide the musicians face or if it was an accident while taken at a concert.  The left side of the photo has a couple of random bright spots that could have been cropped out as well.', '2006-06-05 16:46:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487038, 338938, 56828, '<td valign="top">The photo looks over exposed as opposed to dramatically lit.  You can''t tell what it is you are photography nor where the light is coming from.</td>', 'The photo looks over exposed as opposed to dramatically lit.  You can''t tell what it is you are photography nor where the light is coming from.', '2006-06-05 16:46:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487043, 340183, 56828, '<td valign="top">Challenge related: The reflection in her eyes shows that there are multiple light sources.  Looks to be at least 3 sources.<br/> <br/>Technical: I initially rated this photo lower because of the challenge issue, but the fact is that this is a great photo.  Great sharpness.  The reflection in her eyes adds wonders to this photo.  The technical aspect alone made me rate this photo higher than I would have.</td>', 'Challenge related: The reflection in her eyes shows that there are multiple light sources.  Looks to be at least 3 sources. Technical: I initially rated this photo lower because of the challenge issue, but the fact is that this is a great photo.  Great sharpness.  The reflection in her eyes adds wonders to this photo.  The technical aspect alone made me rate this photo higher than I would have.', '2006-06-05 16:49:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487055, 340763, 45004, '<td valign="top">Very creative look at a chain link fence</td>', 'Very creative look at a chain link fence', '2006-06-05 16:57:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487056, 339204, 56828, '<td valign="top">What is it?  It''s hard to tell if the edges are blurry because of what it is or that was an accident.  Your light kinda spills over on to the floor, but in now real pattern,  I would have liked to seen that part darkened</td>', 'What is it?  It''s hard to tell if the edges are blurry because of what it is or that was an accident.  Your light kinda spills over on to the floor, but in now real pattern,  I would have liked to seen that part darkened', '2006-06-05 16:58:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487059, 340484, 56828, '<td valign="top">There is a little too much contrast between the hairline and the background.  You probably could have used the blur tool to make the hair blend in better with the back ground.</td>', 'There is a little too much contrast between the hairline and the background.  You probably could have used the blur tool to make the hair blend in better with the back ground.', '2006-06-05 17:01:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487070, 340491, 56828, '<td valign="top">Challenge related: The reflection on the containers makes it seem like you have multiple light sources. <br/> <br/>Technical:  The reflection in the containers made it impossible to believe that you were looking at a sunrise in teh kitchen.  Some contrast and darkening of the photo could have made the photo better.</td>', 'Challenge related: The reflection on the containers makes it seem like you have multiple light sources.  Technical:  The reflection in the containers made it impossible to believe that you were looking at a sunrise in teh kitchen.  Some contrast and darkening of the photo could have made the photo better.', '2006-06-05 17:05:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487080, 339886, 56828, '<td valign="top">Challenge related:  The challenge called for an artificial light source, I believe the sun is a natural light source.<br/> <br/>Technical:  The photo is very good.  I like how the bird is sharp and in focus compared to the water.  There is alot of extra space on the left that could have been cropped out.  Another option would to have put the bird in the top right corner, making it seem like it had more room to walk or placing it in the bottom left corner making it seem like the only place to go was into the water.</td>', 'Challenge related:  The challenge called for an artificial light source, I believe the sun is a natural light source. Technical:  The photo is very good.  I like how the bird is sharp and in focus compared to the water.  There is alot of extra space on the left that could have been cropped out.  Another option would to have put the bird in the top right corner, making it seem like it had more room to walk or placing it in the bottom left corner making it seem like the only place to go was into the water.', '2006-06-05 17:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487084, 338686, 59147, '<td valign="top">artificial light?</td>', 'artificial light?', '2006-06-05 17:11:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487086, 340215, 56828, '<td valign="top">Challenge related:  You are using a natural light in a artificial light challenge.<br/> <br/>Technical:  The shot is nice.  The focus is a little soft and a softer light would have worked very well with this photo.  that could have been achieved just by darkening the photo a little.  The portion of the window right about the cat is so bright that it sort of takes away from the cat.</td>', 'Challenge related:  You are using a natural light in a artificial light challenge. Technical:  The shot is nice.  The focus is a little soft and a softer light would have worked very well with this photo.  that could have been achieved just by darkening the photo a little.  The portion of the window right about the cat is so bright that it sort of takes away from the cat.', '2006-06-05 17:12:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487088, 338392, 56828, '<td valign="top">The focus is a tad bit soft.</td>', 'The focus is a tad bit soft.', '2006-06-05 17:12:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487094, 338429, 56828, '<td valign="top">This is a fabulous idea.  I wish the girl were a little bit bigger and more in focus.  Also the lower portion of this photo could hvae been cropped out.  It''s still a great capture.</td>', 'This is a fabulous idea.  I wish the girl were a little bit bigger and more in focus.  Also the lower portion of this photo could hvae been cropped out.  It''s still a great capture.', '2006-06-05 17:15:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487100, 340769, 56828, '<td valign="top">The photo here is too red, and too soft.  More sharpness would have improved the photo.  Maybe even further back to get a capture of the open eye.</td>', 'The photo here is too red, and too soft.  More sharpness would have improved the photo.  Maybe even further back to get a capture of the open eye.', '2006-06-05 17:17:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487109, 340205, 56828, '<td valign="top">This is a nice concept and nice location of your light.  Your background takes away from the photo.  There are too many wrinkles and different types of reflections off the sheet.</td>', 'This is a nice concept and nice location of your light.  Your background takes away from the photo.  There are too many wrinkles and different types of reflections off the sheet.', '2006-06-05 17:19:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487117, 340772, 56828, '<td valign="top">The photo is too pixelated and not very sharp.  You may want to try a smaller ISO.</td>', 'The photo is too pixelated and not very sharp.  You may want to try a smaller ISO.', '2006-06-05 17:21:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487122, 340689, 45004, '<td valign="top">I like the skin textures in this image. I also like the hair over the eyes, yet be able to see the eyes.</td>', 'I like the skin textures in this image. I also like the hair over the eyes, yet be able to see the eyes.', '2006-06-05 17:24:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487126, 339694, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m no fan of such portentous titles, especially when accompanying a portrait, but let that pass. I have a real problem with that small section of her right cheekbone showing - it''s a between-two-stools moment, I think; I get your point, to emphasise the bone structure, but you''ve not completed the job really. Good detail and so on, but that should be a given I think, and the more nebulous and complex elements of an intriguing image aren''t here, for me - almost, perhaps, but that small problem can make a large difference.</td>', 'I''m no fan of such portentous titles, especially when accompanying a portrait, but let that pass. I have a real problem with that small section of her right cheekbone showing - it''s a between-two-stools moment, I think; I get your point, to emphasise the bone structure, but you''ve not completed the job really. Good detail and so on, but that should be a given I think, and the more nebulous and complex elements of an intriguing image aren''t here, for me - almost, perhaps, but that small problem can make a large difference.', '2006-06-05 17:25:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487133, 340147, 6999, '<td valign="top">Lacking composition, really, I''m afraid. Has the feel of un-cropped full frame image which badly needs at least a judicious crop. I don''t see what the immediate appeal is supposed to be, nor do I feel that my eye is guided through the image, and both those elements, I think, have to be strongly present to make such a simple image work.</td>', 'Lacking composition, really, I''m afraid. Has the feel of un-cropped full frame image which badly needs at least a judicious crop. I don''t see what the immediate appeal is supposed to be, nor do I feel that my eye is guided through the image, and both those elements, I think, have to be strongly present to make such a simple image work.', '2006-06-05 17:27:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487144, 340327, 6999, '<td valign="top">There''s some stuff that is nocely done here, although your framing/cropping, I''m afraid, really isn''t part of that. Why on earth cut off the top part of that hammer? Especialloy when all you have in the lower part of frame is the very extremitiy of that vice? The tonality and light are generally good, although the highlights on the hammer''s handle have got out of your control slightly. The feeling that a slightly higher view-point would have solved almost all of those problems is almost unavoidable.</td>', 'There''s some stuff that is nocely done here, although your framing/cropping, I''m afraid, really isn''t part of that. Why on earth cut off the top part of that hammer? Especialloy when all you have in the lower part of frame is the very extremitiy of that vice? The tonality and light are generally good, although the highlights on the hammer''s handle have got out of your control slightly. The feeling that a slightly higher view-point would have solved almost all of those problems is almost unavoidable.', '2006-06-05 17:31:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487155, 338938, 44453, '<td valign="top">I think you''ve got the brown - and I''m guessing that''s what you are aiming for.</td>', 'I think you''ve got the brown - and I''m guessing that''s what you are aiming for.', '2006-06-05 17:34:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487159, 340226, 6999, '<td valign="top">This place has never been kind to blurry photographs, however meaningful they might be; when the composition of them is as apparently random as this - given the drift of colour into the bottom right corner, what is the point of the negative space in the rest of the image? - the voters are likely to be harder on you. There <i>is</i> good stuff here, although it may be better in your own eyes than it is a communication with an audience: for instance, again, that (lack of) cropping. Are we certain that this is the best possible way to present this capture? My answer would be ''no''.</td>', 'This place has never been kind to blurry photographs, however meaningful they might be; when the composition of them is as apparently random as this - given the drift of colour into the bottom right corner, what is the point of the negative space in the rest of the image? - the voters are likely to be harder on you. There is good stuff here, although it may be better in your own eyes than it is a communication with an audience: for instance, again, that (lack of) cropping. Are we certain that this is the best possible way to present this capture? My answer would be ''no''.', '2006-06-05 17:35:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2487345, 340787, 24550, '<td valign="top">i like the composition alot, good use of empty space, and nice rich colors.</td>', 'i like the composition alot, good use of empty space, and nice rich colors.', '2006-06-05 18:12:30.000000', NULL, 1),
