(2495516, 340575, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Not bad for a snap shot from a man obsessed with duct tape LMAO!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I like the use of negative space here. It really helps make the photo meet the challenge description. It works well for you here.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is clear and well defined. No distracting background to worry about.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Color, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Color: I like the B&amp;W treatment. You are right, it works well here.<br/>Focus: pretty darn sharp for handheld at 1/20 second and wide open aperture. Good work on your part handholding the camera for a snapshot.<br/>Light: Overall, I like it and I know you didn''t have much control over it. I have issues with the shadows on her face and that overall her face is dark. Usually I''d suggest a reflector, but that''s probably a bit much to ask for here.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Hell, you know more about that than I do right? ;-) <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Once again good work from you. Keep it up man!<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Not bad for a snap shot from a man obsessed with duct tape LMAO! Composition: I like the use of negative space here. It really helps make the photo meet the challenge description. It works well for you here. Subject: Subject is clear and well defined. No distracting background to worry about. Technical (Color, focus, and light): Color: I like the B&W treatment. You are right, it works well here.Focus: pretty darn sharp for handheld at 1/20 second and wide open aperture. Good work on your part handholding the camera for a snapshot.Light: Overall, I like it and I know you didn''t have much control over it. I have issues with the shadows on her face and that overall her face is dark. Usually I''d suggest a reflector, but that''s probably a bit much to ask for here. To grow its vote?: Hell, you know more about that than I do right? ;-)  Summary: Once again good work from you. Keep it up man! Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-06-07 17:03:02.000000', NULL, 0),
