(2497704, 340121, 22689, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club :</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Sarito !<br/> <br/>Well , first I have to confess that I love cats , they are wonderful !<br/>I have noticed that this one has been your model for different challenges , I hope you see him (?) in more entries , it''s a beautiful cat.<br/> <br/>Back to your photo I think that you could have worked more the post processing as advanced editing was allowed.<br/> <br/>My first impression is that the background is "too" present and as <b>Shutterpug</b> commented the square pattern doesn''t help much.A more neutral background would have centered more the attention on the lovely subject.<br/> <br/>The light you used seems too "strong" , you maybe could have softened it , the shadows are very dark and the chin is burned and as it''s quite centered on the photo I''m quite sure that voters have lowered their votes for this.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to email me about this critique.<br/> <br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club :  Hi Sarito ! Well , first I have to confess that I love cats , they are wonderful !I have noticed that this one has been your model for different challenges , I hope you see him (?) in more entries , it''s a beautiful cat. Back to your photo I think that you could have worked more the post processing as advanced editing was allowed. My first impression is that the background is "too" present and as Shutterpug commented the square pattern doesn''t help much.A more neutral background would have centered more the attention on the lovely subject. The light you used seems too "strong" , you maybe could have softened it , the shadows are very dark and the chin is burned and as it''s quite centered on the photo I''m quite sure that voters have lowered their votes for this. Please feel free to email me about this critique. ', '2006-06-08 03:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497710, 340673, 9668, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> The composition leads the eye straight into the red flowers. There isn''t much else the eye wants to look at, they are immediately drawn into the flowers then stay there. The image looks rather flat to me. The lighting isn''t very dynamic. Maybe it would be more interesting if the lighting was at a slant to create more shadows or if the flashlight was under the flowers to create backlighting. But as it is, there are hardly any shadows, so it isn''t very dynamic.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b>the first thing I notice is that it looks out of focus. Maybe because it was shot at night and probably handheld at 1/6 of a second (a pretty slow shutter speed). I recommend using a tripod for anything slower than 1/50th of a second. I also noticed that you shot this at ISO 400, which caused the noise/graininess. <br/> <br/><b>Overall: </b> I think you have a great idea going here. It has a lot of potential to be an excellent image. If you camera was on a tripod (or something else that could give good stability) and the lighting more dynamic, I think this could have been a great image.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Composition: The composition leads the eye straight into the red flowers. There isn''t much else the eye wants to look at, they are immediately drawn into the flowers then stay there. The image looks rather flat to me. The lighting isn''t very dynamic. Maybe it would be more interesting if the lighting was at a slant to create more shadows or if the flashlight was under the flowers to create backlighting. But as it is, there are hardly any shadows, so it isn''t very dynamic. Technical:the first thing I notice is that it looks out of focus. Maybe because it was shot at night and probably handheld at 1/6 of a second (a pretty slow shutter speed). I recommend using a tripod for anything slower than 1/50th of a second. I also noticed that you shot this at ISO 400, which caused the noise/graininess.  Overall:  I think you have a great idea going here. It has a lot of potential to be an excellent image. If you camera was on a tripod (or something else that could give good stability) and the lighting more dynamic, I think this could have been a great image.', '2006-06-08 03:29:24.000000', NULL, 0),
