(2510235, 338485, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow!   How heartbreaking that this got dq''d!!   I am so sorry!  This is one of the most beautiful maternity photos I''ve ever seen!<br/> <br/>But I hope you will not be too angry with site council either.   There are so, so many members, and there has to be some hard and fast rules.  I had one dq''d too while I was on vacation and couldn''t get to my computer.   It just wasn''t as heartbreaking as this because it wouldn''t have won a ribbon!<br/> <br/>Congratulations anyway on a spectacular photo.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow!   How heartbreaking that this got dq''d!!   I am so sorry!  This is one of the most beautiful maternity photos I''ve ever seen! But I hope you will not be too angry with site council either.   There are so, so many members, and there has to be some hard and fast rules.  I had one dq''d too while I was on vacation and couldn''t get to my computer.   It just wasn''t as heartbreaking as this because it wouldn''t have won a ribbon! Congratulations anyway on a spectacular photo. ', '2006-06-12 18:48:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2510984, 339607, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>My first impression is "Wow!".  This is a very dramatic shot.  The lighting is perfect and the use of black &amp; white really makes this shot.    The composition is excellent. The pose looks as if he is praying, the rope makes me think he is a prisoner of some kind, and the flower tells me that his spirit is unbroken.  All together these elements combine to form a very powerful statement.  You mentioned in your notes that you wanted to capture a "strong image that represents both hope and despair", well I don''t think you truly depict despair.  I believe that this picture shows his spirit triumphing over despair.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your highest scoring entry so far!  However, I feel that this photo deserves a higher score than what you received.  But don''t feel bad about that!  This picture requires the viewer to take some time and think about what they are seeing.  The average voter on DPC spends about 2-3 seconds judging a picture, which means that you only get credit for the first impression.  This photo requires the viewer to soak in what they are seeing, and only then can it''s real impact be appreciated.<br/> <br/>I don''t know how long you have been in photography, but I am really impressed by this shot.  I look forward to seeing more of your work.<br/> <br/>-Bill</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  My first impression is "Wow!".  This is a very dramatic shot.  The lighting is perfect and the use of black & white really makes this shot.    The composition is excellent. The pose looks as if he is praying, the rope makes me think he is a prisoner of some kind, and the flower tells me that his spirit is unbroken.  All together these elements combine to form a very powerful statement.  You mentioned in your notes that you wanted to capture a "strong image that represents both hope and despair", well I don''t think you truly depict despair.  I believe that this picture shows his spirit triumphing over despair. Congratulations on your highest scoring entry so far!  However, I feel that this photo deserves a higher score than what you received.  But don''t feel bad about that!  This picture requires the viewer to take some time and think about what they are seeing.  The average voter on DPC spends about 2-3 seconds judging a picture, which means that you only get credit for the first impression.  This photo requires the viewer to soak in what they are seeing, and only then can it''s real impact be appreciated. I don''t know how long you have been in photography, but I am really impressed by this shot.  I look forward to seeing more of your work. -Bill', '2006-06-13 00:12:35.000000', NULL, 0),
