(2522871, 340621, 31794, '<td valign="top">[[trading post]] <br/> <br/>very nice, composition, color and postprocessing seems pretty good.<br/> <br/>too bad the woody is used so much that images of woody usually get lower scores unless they are extrodinary, wich yours unfortunately isn´t.<br/> <br/>at least you got in the top 100  :)</td>', '[[trading post]]  very nice, composition, color and postprocessing seems pretty good. too bad the woody is used so much that images of woody usually get lower scores unless they are extrodinary, wich yours unfortunately isn´t. at least you got in the top 100  :)', '2006-06-16 16:36:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2526347, 339433, 34659, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot - lovely color tones and leading lines/curves.  Very appealing visually and effective use of black background to emphasize your subject.  I didn''t vote in this challenge but would have probably scored this an 8.  The only things I see that I would try to improve are a couple of spots in the background (easily cloned or blended out) and a little stronger focus on the actual tulips themselves.  Well done.  Love the peach color.</td>', 'Beautiful shot - lovely color tones and leading lines/curves.  Very appealing visually and effective use of black background to emphasize your subject.  I didn''t vote in this challenge but would have probably scored this an 8.  The only things I see that I would try to improve are a couple of spots in the background (easily cloned or blended out) and a little stronger focus on the actual tulips themselves.  Well done.  Love the peach color.', '2006-06-18 15:35:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2527818, 340786, 49202, '<td valign="top"><b>CPTII</b> <br/> <br/>Actually, the shot looks better the longer you stare at it.<br/>It was a great idea, albeit not very obvious e.g. the low DNMC scores.<br/>The subject was, honestly, still a bit too dark. A 30-second expsure with a 1-second exposure for the light would''ve looked better, I think.<br/>Just a suggestion, though.</td>', 'CPTII  Actually, the shot looks better the longer you stare at it.It was a great idea, albeit not very obvious e.g. the low DNMC scores.The subject was, honestly, still a bit too dark. A 30-second expsure with a 1-second exposure for the light would''ve looked better, I think.Just a suggestion, though.', '2006-06-19 05:32:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2528882, 340786, 24503, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from Álex, CTP MkII </b> <br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b>: very clever idea but IMO the realization could be improved<br/><b>Composition</b>: good, in this case the centered composition works well<br/><b>Subject</b>: very good concept for the challenge, with an original idea<br/><b>Technical</b>: the main flaw IMO is technical. If you had achieved a good silhouette, this shoot will deserved a very high score. <br/><b>Improvement</b>: a better lighting to make the silhouette more perfect<br/><b>Summary</b>: very intelligent idea.<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'Hello from Álex, CTP MkII   First Impression: very clever idea but IMO the realization could be improvedComposition: good, in this case the centered composition works wellSubject: very good concept for the challenge, with an original ideaTechnical: the main flaw IMO is technical. If you had achieved a good silhouette, this shoot will deserved a very high score. Improvement: a better lighting to make the silhouette more perfectSummary: very intelligent idea. Álex', '2006-06-19 14:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2529200, 338485, 59006, '<td valign="top">Dear Ursula &amp; Shannon,<br/> <br/>Thanks for your help on technical issues.<br/> <br/>As the consul requested the RAW file has been sent to the consul at this moment. I simply want to clarify all the commotion. Did this happen before? Did a ribbon got DQ''ed? <br/> <br/>I hope that this will clear the matters for once and stop several asumptions and discussions at the forum about my shot, who I might be, and how much I had acess to the internet during my New York trip.<br/> <br/>I had not much internet access thoughout the trip. Only on few occasions for a short period of time.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Hera<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ursula:</b></div><hr/><i> I did not DQ the picture, we did it as SC.  I sent you a PM as a courtesy, asking if there was a way we could help you to validate the image - neither I nor SC got an answer.  The letter to me that is in your image details was never sent to me or to SC.<br/> <br/>The reason we need an original is to verify that the image was made during the times allowed.  It''s that simple. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Dear Ursula & Shannon, Thanks for your help on technical issues. As the consul requested the RAW file has been sent to the consul at this moment. I simply want to clarify all the commotion. Did this happen before? Did a ribbon got DQ''ed?  I hope that this will clear the matters for once and stop several asumptions and discussions at the forum about my shot, who I might be, and how much I had acess to the internet during my New York trip. I had not much internet access thoughout the trip. Only on few occasions for a short period of time. Regards, Hera Originally posted by ursula: I did not DQ the picture, we did it as SC.  I sent you a PM as a courtesy, asking if there was a way we could help you to validate the image - neither I nor SC got an answer.  The letter to me that is in your image details was never sent to me or to SC. The reason we need an original is to verify that the image was made during the times allowed.  It''s that simple. ', '2006-06-19 16:41:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2529470, 340689, 41337, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2</b> <br/> <br/>Dark images is what this challenge is all about and this came out pretty good. I''m actually surprised this did decent at DPC. I really don''t have any suggestions other than to keep working on that look. I tend to favor more detail so for me I would have liked to see a bit more of that in your eyes. Not so much those fancy retinas everyone has in their photos but give me more bursting capillaries! :P<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-19 17:26:07.</i></td>', 'Greetings from CTP2  Dark images is what this challenge is all about and this came out pretty good. I''m actually surprised this did decent at DPC. I really don''t have any suggestions other than to keep working on that look. I tend to favor more detail so for me I would have liked to see a bit more of that in your eyes. Not so much those fancy retinas everyone has in their photos but give me more bursting capillaries! :P', '2006-06-19 18:25:10.000000', '2006-06-19 18:26:07.000000', 0),
(2529674, 338485, 5508, '<td valign="top">That sucks, the same thing happened to me. AND I SENT MY RAW IMAGE before I left for my vacation. No one got back to me before I left.<br/> <br/>BTW I gave your image a 10.</td>', 'That sucks, the same thing happened to me. AND I SENT MY RAW IMAGE before I left for my vacation. No one got back to me before I left. BTW I gave your image a 10.', '2006-06-19 19:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2529795, 338485, 36006, '<td valign="top">Hera,<br/> <br/>I can see great things comming from you. This DQ should only be viewed as a minor setback.<br/> <br/>I would think the next time you leave behind any submissions in the future, that you have a plan to qualify future requests from SC.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the future.</td>', 'Hera, I can see great things comming from you. This DQ should only be viewed as a minor setback. I would think the next time you leave behind any submissions in the future, that you have a plan to qualify future requests from SC. Good luck in the future.', '2006-06-19 20:12:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2533147, 340770, 37893, '<td valign="top">Whoa! Talk about major burning for this image! I actually like it a lot. It has an eerie feel to it. Not quite sure about the tilt of the lens but it does add a dynamic effect to the image.</td>', 'Whoa! Talk about major burning for this image! I actually like it a lot. It has an eerie feel to it. Not quite sure about the tilt of the lens but it does add a dynamic effect to the image.', '2006-06-20 21:47:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2536222, 340784, 39349, '<td valign="top">This shot is so bad ass I can''t even begin to tell you! I gave this a 10 during voting and I have to say is one of my top favs from your work and on this site. AMAZING work!<br/> <br/></td>', 'This shot is so bad ass I can''t even begin to tell you! I gave this a 10 during voting and I have to say is one of my top favs from your work and on this site. AMAZING work! ', '2006-06-21 12:08:52.000000', NULL, 0),
